NoMercy: on an Intel Mac, register ggml's Metal device only when the default
GPU can run the backend well.

ggml's Metal backend is built for both Macs. Apple Silicon is untouched. On
x86_64 the default device must report the Metal 3 GPU family and must not be
an integrated (low power) GPU; otherwise the backend registers no device and
every filter stays on the CPU, as all releases up to v1.0.49 did there.
Without Metal 3 ggml_metal_device_supports_op() refuses the matrix products
and the graph bounces between GPU and CPU. NOMERCY_GGML_METAL=1 takes the
default device regardless (for measuring a GPU this rule leaves out).

Applied by scripts/48-whisper.sh to the pinned v1.9.1 checkout, after the
residency-sets sed. Not sent upstream: upstream offers the device on every
Mac and leaves the choice to the application.

